Details of parsing:
arXiv abs HTML: 
- title: regex `<h1 class="title mathjax"><span class="descriptor">Title:</span>(.*?)</h1>` strip tags.
- abstract: `<blockquote class="abstract mathjax">\s*<span class="descriptor">Abstract:</span>(.*?)</blockquote>` strip tags.
- authors: `<div class="authors"><span class="descriptor">Authors:</span>(.*?)</div>` strip tags.
- submission history: `<div class="submission-history">...` contains dates like `[Submitted on 5 Jan 2018 (v1), last revised ...]`. Title date parse may be messy but can extract "Submitted on ...".

Crossref JSON: message.title[0], message.author[*].family, message['container-title'][0], message.issued/published date-parts.

Comparison logic:
- normalize(text): lowercase, collapse whitespace, strip punctuation variants.
- title_match: normalized ledger title == normalized fetched title, or one is a prefix of the other (title truncation), or first 40 chars equal.
- first_author_match: ledger authors' first surname appears in fetched authors (and vice versa).
- year: ledger year int vs fetched candidate years: crossref issued year, published-print year, published-online year; arxiv submission year. MATCH if any equals ledger; PARTIAL if only online-first year equals ledger-1 or ledger+1; else MISMATCH... Actually flash-10 treated year convention as PARTIAL. I'll classify: if title+author match and year matches within ±1 → MATCH with note if not exact; if no year info fetched → PARTIAL.
- venue: crossref container-title tokens vs ledger venue; or arXiv presence vs ledger venue including "arXiv:...". Compare loosely: if any significant token of container title appears in ledger venue → venue_match. PARTIAL if not comparable.
- excerpt: compare ledger evidence_excerpt (strip "Abstract:" prefix and quotes) to fetched abstract: token overlap (e.g., first 8 words present). Since excerpt may be truncated/modified, compute similarity via difflib ratio on normalized strings; MATCH if ratio>0.6 or first-10-word match; PARTIAL if 0.3-0.6; MISMATCH if <0.3.

Verdict: 
- FETCH_FAILED if fetch error/non-200/work-not-found.
- MISMATCH if title mismatch or first author mismatch.
